Here's the full implementation for all three: wallet-as-store-credit at checkout, admin top-up page, and admin-only access locked to your account.
Architecture Summary
Concern	Solution
Wallet spendable at checkout	Extend perform_spin-style RPC to apply_wallet_to_order; wallet debit + order insert in one transaction
Admin page access	Three-layer defense: (1) hardcoded ADMIN_EMAILS env var, (2) RLS policy is_admin() Postgres function, (3) client-side route guard
Admin top-ups	admin_credit_wallet RPC — callable only by service role OR admin user via is_admin() check inside the function

The key security principle: the client never sends "credit this user R100" and gets trusted. Every wallet mutation re-validates auth.uid() against the admin list inside Postgres. Even if someone steals your anon key and calls the RPC manually from DevTools, the function rejects them.
1. Database: Admin Role + Wallet-At-Checkout

